hese two points. Let's find its equation.\n\nSlope of KM: (1/2 -4/5)/(sqrt(3)/2 - (-3/5)) = (5/10 -8/10)/(sqrt(3)/2 +3/5) = (-3/10)/( (5sqrt(3) +6)/10 )= (-3)/(5sqrt(3)+6).\n\nThat's messy, but let's parametrize it. Let\u2019s parameterize line KM.\n\nParametric equations:\n\nx = -3/5 + t*(sqrt(3)/2 +3/5 )\n\ny = 4/5 + t*(1/2 -4/5 ) =4/5 + t*(-3/10)\n\nWe need to find t such that y = -sqrt(3)x +1.\n\nSo:\n\n4/5 - (3/10)t = -sqrt(3)[ -3/5 + t*(sqrt(3)/2 +3/5 ) ] +1\n\nLet me compute RHS:\n\n-sqrt(3)*(-3/5) + -sqrt(3)*t*(sqrt(3)/2 +3/5 ) +1\n\n= (3 sqrt(3)/5) + -sqrt(3)*t*(sqrt(3)/2 +3/5 ) +1\n\nNow, let's expand the term with t:\n\n-sqrt(3)*t*sqrt(3)/2 - sqrt(3)*t*3/5 = - (3t/2) - (3 sqrt(3) t)/5\n\nSo RHS = 3 sqrt(3)/5 +1 - 3t/2 - 3 sqrt(3) t /5\n\nThus, equation becomes:\n\n4/5 - (3/10)t = 3 sqrt(3)/5 +1 - 3t/2 - 3 sqrt(3) t /5\n\nLet me multiply both sides by 10 to eliminate denominators:\n\n8 -3t = 6 sqrt(3) +10 -15t -6 sqrt(3) t\n\nBring all terms to left side:\n\n8 -3t -6 sqrt(3) -10 +15t +6 sqrt(3) t =0\n\nSimplify:\n\n(-2) +12t +6 sqrt(3) t -6 sqrt(3)=0\n\nFactor t:\n\n12t +6 sqrt(3) t =6 sqrt(3) +2\n\nt(12 +6 sqrt(3))=6 sqrt(3) +2\n\nt=(6 sqrt(3)+2)/(12 +6 sqrt(3))= [2(3 sqrt(3)+1)]/[6(2 + sqrt(3))] = (3 sqrt(3)+1)/(3(2 + sqrt(3)))\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by (2 - sqrt(3)):\n\nt= (3 sqrt(3)+1)(2 - sqrt(3))/(3*(4 -3))= (3 sqrt(3)+1)(2 - sqrt(3))/(3*1)\n\nCompute numerator:\n\n3 sqrt(3)*2 -3 sqrt(3)*sqrt(3) +1*2 -1*sqrt(3)=6 sqrt(3) -9 +2 -sqrt(3)= (6 sqrt(3)-sqrt(3)) + (-9+2)=5 sqrt(3) -7\n\nThus, t=(5 sqrt(3) -7)/3\n\nSo, x-coordinate of P:\n\nx = -3/5 + t*(sqrt(3)/2 +3/5 )\n\nPlug in t=(5 sqrt(3) -7)/3\n\nFirst, compute sqrt(3)/2 +3/5 = (5 sqrt(3) +6)/10\n\nThus,\n\nx= -3/5 + (5 sqrt(3) -7)/3 * (5 sqrt(3) +6)/10\n\nLet me compute (5 sqrt(3) -7)(5 sqrt(3) +6):\n\n= (5 sqrt(3))\u00b2 +5 sqrt(3)*6 -7*5 sqrt(3) -7*6\n\n=75 +30 sqrt(3) -35 sqrt(3) -42\n\n=75 -42 + (30 sqrt(3) -35 sqrt(3))\n\n=33 -5 sqrt(3)\n\nThus,\n\nx= -3/5 + (33 -5 sqrt(3))/30 = 